From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Zinchenko <m1d3ry@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:39:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Replace the MSIXResource CMake templates with the pack-only
 files

CMake fills `MSIXResource.hpp.cmakein` and `MSIXResource.cpp.cmakein` with the trusted-root
certificates and the XSD schemas, as a ZIP byte array. A pack-only build never reads that blob.
`AppxFactory` copies it without a parse, and only the non-skip branch of `SignatureValidator` looks at
the certificates. A build that packs with `MSIX_VALIDATION_OPTION_SKIPSIGNATURE` therefore needs no
resource at all.

Commit the two files with the "no resource files" fallback of `cmake/msix_resources.cmake`, which is one
0x00 byte, and with empty `GetResources` bodies. The schema namespace manager is empty for the same
reason. It keys on `wchar_t` for the msxml6 parser and on `char` for the xerces parser, so one
preprocessor branch on `USING_MSXML` covers both.

This lets a build system compile the SDK with no template expansion step. It removes the two
`.cmakein` files, so the CMake build no longer works. Do not send this commit upstream.
